  "title": "Merge origin/main (PR 21, context active paths) into goal/T-0861 (skills program): resolve the three conflicts keeping both programs' behaviour, full gate green",
  "spec": "PR 22 (goal/T-0861 \u2192 main) conflicts with main after PR 21 merged (5646e4b). Dry run: `git merge --no-ff origin/main` into goal/T-0861 conflicts in orchestrator/promotion.py, orchestrator/spawn.py and tests/test_executor.py. Both sides are wanted: main brings the context program's active paths (context router active with routed packet sections and recovery logging, tool disclosure active with the minimal allowlist and the needs_tool escalation, handoff-aware routing, read suppression) and promotion features for them; goal/T-0861 brings the skills program (skill routing shadow/active, the skills packet section presented first, specialists, skill_routing/jev_skill_routing promotion features, telemetry keys).\nDo, in the worktree the daemon gives you (it is based on goal/T-0861): `git fetch origin` then `git merge --no-ff origin/main`; resolve each conflict by keeping BOTH sides' additions (every FEATURES entry, every collect() branch, both packet builders' additional keyword arguments, every test), never dropping a function, a mode key or a test; where both sides changed the same function (spawn.packet / review_packet keyword lists, run_worker's launch argv and result handling, _dispatch paths), integrate them so that: the skills section stays the first packet section, the routed sections replace only the router's sections, tool disclosure's minimal allowlist and the skills' --disable-slash-commands both apply in their active modes, and the escalation respawn runs once. Keep every mode at its current value in pool.toml (merge the tables). Run `.claude/hooks/tests-green.sh .` until green (the union of both suites, ~1230 tests), then `uv run orchestrator context-eval` and `uv run orchestrator skill-eval` must both exit 0. Commit the merge on the task branch (a merge commit is expected here; message starts with the task id). Do not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main HEAD holds in the worktree (main is merged in)",
    "no conflict markers remain; `.claude/hooks/tests-green.sh .` exits 0",
